


# ---- Conventional Commits 1.0.0 -----------------------------------
#
#   <type>[(<scope>)][!]: <description>
#
#   [body]
#
#   [footer(s)]
#
# subject   imperative mood, lower case, no trailing period, <= 50 chars
# body      wrap at 72; explain what changed and why, not how
#
# type
#   feat      new feature (MINOR)
#   fix       bug fix (PATCH)
#   docs      documentation only
#   style     formatting, no code change
#   refactor  neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf      performance improvement
#   test      adding or correcting tests
#   build     build system or dependencies
#   ci        CI config and scripts
#   chore     other changes, no src or test files
#   revert    reverts a previous commit
#
# scope     optional noun for the affected area:  feat(parser): ...
#
# breaking  append ! before the colon:  feat(api)!: drop v1 endpoints
#           and/or add a footer:        BREAKING CHANGE: <what and why>
#           either form means MAJOR
#
# footers   Refs: #123
#           Closes: #123
#           Co-authored-by: Name <email>
#
# examples
#   feat(auth): add refresh token rotation
#   fix: guard against empty pathspec
#   docs(readme): document config.local setup
#   refactor(lf)!: rename preview hook arguments
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
